; REQUEST-09 boundary: the collapsed-set instance is bound to a NAMED rule the author wrote
; (`named_set = set<key_hash>`, ident `NamedSet`), not an anonymous field-site instance. A named
; rule keeps its own wasm class and the criterion-8 #3 contract: a consumer requesting the
; structural `[* key_hash]` (KeyHashList) collides with the dep's own `NamedSet` producer and must
; hard-error with a remedy the author can act on (rename / @name / drop the rule).
key_hash = bytes ; @newtype
set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0]
named_set = set<key_hash>
cert = [pool_owners: named_set]
